<p><strong>Draft version:</strong> {{ config('legal.privacy_notice_version') }} · <strong>Last updated:</strong> November 16, 2026</p>
<p>This draft is intended for review against the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173) and its Implementing Rules and Regulations. It is not a claim that Lumora has been assessed or confirmed compliant. See the <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/DATA-PRIVACY-ACT/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Privacy Commission's text of the Act</a>.</p>

<h2>1. Personal Information Collected</h2>
<p>Based on the current registration form, Lumora collects your name, sex, date of birth, email address, telephone number, and delivery address. It also processes your password, verification status, and registration consent record. If you apply to sell, the seller application may request business details and supporting documents. When you use the marketplace, further information may be created or collected about listings, orders, messages, reviews, returns, and support requests. Technical information such as device, browser, log, and session data may also be processed by the service. Lumora must verify this list against its deployed systems and vendors before publication.</p>

<h2>2. Purpose of Data Collection</h2>
<p>Information is collected only for specific purposes that Lumora should document, including account creation and administration, age and email verification, seller application review, displaying and fulfilling orders, customer support, marketplace safety, and meeting applicable legal obligations. Fields that are not needed for a stated purpose should not be collected.</p>

<h2>3. How Personal Information Is Used</h2>
<p>Information may be used to authenticate your account, send verification and service messages, process marketplace activity, connect an order with the relevant seller and delivery process, prevent misuse, and respond to your requests. Optional marketing should remain optional and separate from information needed to provide the service. Lumora should confirm its actual analytics, marketing, payment, and automated decision practices before publishing this draft.</p>

<h2>4. Data Storage and Security</h2>
<p>Lumora should describe the actual technical, organizational, and physical safeguards used to protect personal information, including safeguards applied by service providers. This draft does not assert that any particular certification, security control, hosting location, or breach response has been independently verified. Access should be limited to authorized purposes, and passwords should not be stored in readable form.</p>

<h2>5. Sharing of Personal Information</h2>
<p>Information may need to be shared with the seller handling an order and with delivery, hosting, communications, payment, or other service providers where they are actually used and the disclosure is necessary for the stated purpose or otherwise allowed by law. Lumora should identify the relevant recipients or recipient categories, their roles, and any cross-border processing before publication. Personal information should not be sold as a general practice; any separate data sharing must be disclosed and supported by an appropriate lawful basis.</p>

<h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
<p>Lumora should retain personal information only for as long as needed for the disclosed purpose, applicable legal obligations, or the establishment, exercise, or defense of legal claims, and then securely dispose of or anonymize it where appropriate. Exact retention periods for accounts, orders, verification records, seller documents, support records, and logs have not been supplied and must be determined before publication.</p>

<h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
<p>Subject to the Data Privacy Act and its rules, data subjects have rights that may include being informed, access, object, rectification, erasure or blocking in applicable cases, damages, filing a complaint with the National Privacy Commission, and data portability where applicable. Rights may have legal conditions or exceptions. You may also withdraw consent where processing is based on consent; withdrawal does not affect processing already carried out on another valid basis. Lumora must publish a real channel and process for requests before this notice is finalized. More information is available from the <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph/data-subject-rights/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Privacy Commission's data subject rights page</a>.</p>

<h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
<p>Lumora's legal entity or personal information controller identity, Data Protection Officer (if designated), privacy contact details, and request channel have not been provided. These must be completed and verified before this notice is published. Do not rely on this draft to submit a privacy request; use Lumora's verified contact channel once one is published.</p>

<h2>9. Changes to This Notice</h2>
<p>Lumora should publish the effective date and version of a finalized notice and explain material changes. Where required, it should provide notice or seek consent before applying changes to personal information processing.</p>
